# mpd-virt.env — your own settings, shared by every mpd VM you run.
#
# Put a setting here to apply it to all your projects, everywhere. A
# single project overrides it in its own /srv/projects/<name>/mpd.env.
#
# Every line below is commented out. Uncomment the ones you want and give
# them your values. A change takes effect on the next command — nothing to
# restart, nothing to sync.
#
# Which copy do you edit?
#
#   On a Mac that runs mpd-virt, edit ~/.mpd-virt/mpd-virt.env. mpd-virt
#   pushes it into every VM you own when you take one over, start it, or
#   update it. That Mac holds the only copy worth editing: the file here
#   in the VM is replaced on the next push.
#
#   On a sandbox VM, nothing pushes anything, so edit this file directly.
#   It is yours.
#
# Where these settings sit among the others, and which file wins when two
# disagree: docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, section 8.


# PHP version
#
# One of: 8.1, 8.2, 8.3, 8.4, 8.5. Applies to every PHP project type,
# which today means Moodle. The default is in
# /opt/mpd/assets/runtime/mpd-defaults.env.
#MPD_PHP_VERSION=8.4


# Installing a Moodle site
#
# `mdl-install` asks for these when you do not set them. Set them once
# here and the install runs without stopping to ask.
#MPD_MOODLE_AGREE_LICENSE=1
#MPD_MOODLE_ADMINPASS=Admin.1234
#MPD_MOODLE_ADMINEMAIL=admin@example.com


# PHPUnit
#
# Set this to 1 to also run the tests that need external services —
# redis, memcached, solr, ldap. They are skipped otherwise.
#MPD_MOODLE_PHPUNIT_EXTERNAL_SERVICES=1


# Behat
#
# Set this to 1 to run the browser without a window. Faster, and it does
# not take over your screen while a test runs.
#MPD_MOODLE_BEHAT_BROWSER_HEADLESS=1


# Xdebug
#
# One of: off, debug, profile, coverage, trace.
# Rebuild the runtime after changing it: mpd --runtime-rebuild
#MPD_XDEBUG_MODE=off


# Running mpd from inside a runtime container
#
# Set this to off to stop `mpd init|start|stop|delete|status`
# from working inside a runtime. Leave it alone and those commands work
# there, on the projects that belong to that runtime.
#
# Turn it off to limit the damage a runaway AI agent can do. A runtime is
# where agents run, with passwordless sudo. While this is on, an agent
# there can delete a project — its database, its dataroot and its source
# tree — not only edit files. It can never create or delete databases,
# rebuild the runtime, or run any --vm-*, --runtime-* or --service-*
# command. See docs/SECURITY.md.
#
# Only off, false, 0 and no switch it off. A typo leaves it on, so that a
# slip cannot quietly break mpd inside every runtime.
#
# Read on every command, so a change applies to the next one.
#MPD_RUNTIME_CONTROL=off
